# RARO MARK

## Origin

The RARO Mark is derived from an ancient Mesopotamian rosette motif.

Rather than reproducing the historical symbol directly, the form was studied, abstracted, and refined into a contemporary mark.

The result is a symbol that connects heritage with modernity.

A mark rooted in history but designed for the present.

---

## Meaning

The circular form represents continuity.

The central void represents possibility.

The surrounding elements represent the marks left by time, culture, memory, and human presence.

Together they form the visual signature of the archive.

---

## Function

The RARO Mark is the primary brand symbol.

It represents the archive itself rather than any individual collection.

---

## Usage

The RARO Mark appears only on:

- Front chest prints
- Packaging
- Hang tags
- Labels
- Brand communication

---

## Restrictions

The RARO Mark must never be:

- Redrawn
- Reinterpreted
- Distorted
- Stretched
- Simplified
- Replaced

The approved master reference must always be used.

---

## Relationship to Collections

The RARO Mark belongs to the archive.

Collection symbols belong to their respective concepts.

RARO Mark = Brand Identity

Collection Symbol = Collection Identit
